==Battleground==
*2 [[Two Can]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is incredibly simple, with the only threat essentially being the Two Cans. If you have [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat) |Royal Guard Cat]], you can use [[Biohazard (Combo) | Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo) | Bony Bone]] and Royal Guard solos the stage.

If not, you can support him or just use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat) | Octopus]] with units such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)| Courier]] to destroy the Two Cans, along with something to deal with the squirrels such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat) | Slapsticks]].

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Uber Rare Cats from the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]] set: Cheap and spammable on 1st form, which will work well on taking out the squirrels.
*[[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]]/[[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Tokyo Miku]]: A safer Octopus Cat thanks to their standing range.
*Long Distance Ubers: They're able to hit the Two Cans even if squirrels get in the way of their attacks.
*[[Imagawa Yoshimoto (Uber Rare Cat)|Imagawa Yoshimoto]]/[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]]: phenomenal picks for this stage, since Yoshimoto deals good damage to the Two Can + [[Weaken]]s it, and Saber is cheap for an uber and easily gets rid of the squirrels.

